5G-LENA (NR v3.3), model/nr-ue-mac.{cc,h}: the retxBSR-Timer of TS 38.321 (5.4.5), which the library does not have.

A UE tells the gNB how much data it has waiting with a buffer status report, carried inside its uplink transport
blocks, and asks for a first grant with a scheduling request. The library's UE sends a scheduling request only when
data arrives while its request state is INACTIVE, and leaves that state only when a grant has emptied its buffer.
If the transport block that carries the last buffer status report is lost (all HARQ transmissions fail, or the HARQ
process expires), the gNB believes the buffer is empty and grants nothing, while the UE still has data and is
waiting for a grant: nothing is sent by that UE for the rest of the simulation. In a real UE the retxBSR-Timer ends
this: when it expires with data still waiting, the buffer status report is triggered again, and with no grant to
carry it, a scheduling request is sent.

The change: the UE remembers when it last received an uplink grant (or sent a scheduling request); if it has data
waiting and that is longer ago than RetxBsrTimer (new attribute of ns3::NrUeMac, default 80 ms, 0 = off), it sends
the scheduling request again.

Found with the frequency-division scheduler, where transport blocks were lost in numbers; 3 of 80 simulated UAVs at
8 per cell and 26 of 160 at 16 per cell went silent for good.

Applied by simulation/run_sweep.py (once; `git -C ns-3-dev/contrib/nr apply`).

diff --git a/model/nr-ue-mac.cc b/model/nr-ue-mac.cc
index db73b268..53872646 100644
--- a/model/nr-ue-mac.cc
+++ b/model/nr-ue-mac.cc
@@ -214,6 +214,12 @@ NrUeMac::GetTypeId()
                 UintegerValue(16),
                 MakeUintegerAccessor(&NrUeMac::SetNumHarqProcess, &NrUeMac::GetNumHarqProcess),
                 MakeUintegerChecker<uint8_t>())
+            .AddAttribute("RetxBsrTimer",
+                          "retxBSR-Timer (TS 38.321, 5.4.5): with data waiting and no uplink grant for this "
+                          "long, the scheduling request is sent again. Zero disables it.",
+                          TimeValue(MilliSeconds(80)),
+                          MakeTimeAccessor(&NrUeMac::m_retxBsrTimer),
+                          MakeTimeChecker())
             .AddTraceSource("UeMacRxedCtrlMsgsTrace",
                             "Ue MAC Control Messages Traces.",
                             MakeTraceSourceAccessor(&NrUeMac::m_macRxedCtrlMsgsTrace),
@@ -552,6 +558,17 @@ NrUeMac::DoSlotIndication(const SfnSf& sfn)
         NS_LOG_INFO("Sending SR to PHY in slot " << sfn);
         SendSR();
         m_srState = ACTIVE;
+        m_lastUlGrant = Simulator::Now();
+    }
+    else if (m_srState == ACTIVE && !m_retxBsrTimer.IsZero() && GetTotalBufSize() > 0 &&
+             Simulator::Now() - m_lastUlGrant >= m_retxBsrTimer)
+    {
+        // Kyber-6G: retxBSR-Timer. Data is waiting, a scheduling request was sent, and no grant has come since.
+        // The gNB believes this UE's buffer is empty (the transport block with the last buffer status report
+        // was lost), and without asking again the UE would wait forever.
+        NS_LOG_INFO("retxBSR-Timer expired with " << GetTotalBufSize() << " bytes waiting: sending SR again");
+        SendSR();
+        m_lastUlGrant = Simulator::Now();
     }
 
     // Feedback missing
@@ -671,6 +688,7 @@ NrUeMac::ProcessUlDci(const Ptr<NrUlDciMessage>& dciMsg)
     m_ulDciSfnsf = dataSfn;
     m_ulDciTotalUsed = 0;
     m_ulDci = dciMsg->GetDciInfoElement();
+    m_lastUlGrant = Simulator::Now();
 
     m_macRxedCtrlMsgsTrace(m_currentSlot, GetCellId(), m_rnti, GetBwpId(), dciMsg);
 
diff --git a/model/nr-ue-mac.h b/model/nr-ue-mac.h
index 16e5a037..e3f3946b 100644
--- a/model/nr-ue-mac.h
+++ b/model/nr-ue-mac.h
@@ -417,6 +417,8 @@ class NrUeMac : public Object
     };
 
     SrBsrMachine m_srState{INACTIVE}; //!< Current state for the SR/BSR machine.
+    Time m_retxBsrTimer{MilliSeconds(80)}; //!< retxBSR-Timer: ask for a grant again after this long without one
+    Time m_lastUlGrant{Seconds(0)};        //!< When the last uplink grant arrived (or the last SR was sent)
 
     Ptr<UniformRandomVariable> m_raPreambleUniformVariable;
     uint8_t m_raPreambleId{0}; //!< The RA Preamble ID
